---@field WeightedCapacity? aws.emr.WholeNumber The number of units that a provisioned instance of this type provides toward fulfilling the target capacities defined in InstanceFleetConfig. Capacity values represent performance characteristics such as vCPUs, memory, or I/O. If not specified, the default value is 1.
---@field BidPrice? aws.emr.XmlStringMaxLen256 The bid price for each Amazon EC2 Spot Instance type as defined by InstanceType. Expressed in USD. If neither BidPrice nor BidPriceAsPercentageOfOnDemandPrice is provided, BidPriceAsPercentageOfOnDemandPrice defaults to 100%.
---@field BidPriceAsPercentageOfOnDemandPrice? aws.emr.NonNegativeDouble The bid price, as a percentage of On-Demand price, for each Amazon EC2 Spot Instance as defined by InstanceType. Expressed as a number (for example, 20 specifies 20%).
---@field Configurations? aws.emr.ConfigurationList A configuration classification that applies when provisioning cluster instances, which can include configurations for applications and software bundled with Amazon EMR.
---@field EbsBlockDevices? aws.emr.EbsBlockDeviceList The configuration of Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) attached to each instance as defined by InstanceType.
---@field EbsOptimized? aws.emr.BooleanObject Evaluates to TRUE when the specified InstanceType is EBS-optimized.
---@field CustomAmiId? aws.emr.XmlStringMaxLen256 The custom AMI ID to use for the instance type.
---@field Priority? aws.emr.NonNegativeDouble The priority at which Amazon EMR launches the Amazon EC2 instances with this instance type. Priority starts at 0, which is the highest priority. Amazon EMR considers the highest priority first.

