---@field InstanceFleets? aws.emr.InstanceFleetConfigList The instance fleet configuration is available only in Amazon EMR releases 4.8.0 and later, excluding 5.0.x versions. Describes the Amazon EC2 instances and instance configurations for clusters that use the instance fleet configuration.
---@field Ec2KeyName? aws.emr.XmlStringMaxLen256 The name of the Amazon EC2 key pair that can be used to connect to the master node using SSH as the user called "hadoop."
---@field Placement? aws.emr.PlacementType The Availability Zone in which the cluster runs.
---@field KeepJobFlowAliveWhenNoSteps? aws.emr.Boolean Specifies whether the cluster should remain available after completing all steps. Defaults to false. For more information about configuring cluster termination, see Control Cluster Termination in the EMR Management Guide.
---@field TerminationProtected? aws.emr.Boolean Specifies whether to lock the cluster to prevent the Amazon EC2 instances from being terminated by API call, user intervention, or in the event of a job-flow error.
---@field UnhealthyNodeReplacement? aws.emr.BooleanObject Indicates whether Amazon EMR should gracefully replace core nodes that have degraded within the cluster.
---@field HadoopVersion? aws.emr.XmlStringMaxLen256 Applies only to Amazon EMR release versions earlier than 4.0. The Hadoop version for the cluster. Valid inputs are "0.18" (no longer maintained), "0.20" (no longer maintained), "0.20.205" (no longer maintained), "1.0.3", "2.2.0", or "2.4.0". If you do not set this value, the default of 0.18 is used, unless the AmiVersion parameter is set in the RunJobFlow call, in which case the default version of...
---@field Ec2SubnetId? aws.emr.XmlStringMaxLen256 Applies to clusters that use the uniform instance group configuration. To launch the cluster in Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC), set this parameter to the identifier of the Amazon VPC subnet where you want the cluster to launch. If you do not specify this value and your account supports EC2-Classic, the cluster launches in EC2-Classic.
---@field Ec2SubnetIds? aws.emr.XmlStringMaxLen256List Applies to clusters that use the instance fleet configuration. When multiple Amazon EC2 subnet IDs are specified, Amazon EMR evaluates them and launches instances in the optimal subnet.
---@field EmrManagedMasterSecurityGroup? aws.emr.XmlStringMaxLen256 The identifier of the Amazon EC2 security group for the master node. If you specify EmrManagedMasterSecurityGroup, you must also specify EmrManagedSlaveSecurityGroup.
---@field EmrManagedSlaveSecurityGroup? aws.emr.XmlStringMaxLen256 The identifier of the Amazon EC2 security group for the core and task nodes. If you specify EmrManagedSlaveSecurityGroup, you must also specify EmrManagedMasterSecurityGroup.
---@field ServiceAccessSecurityGroup? aws.emr.XmlStringMaxLen256 The identifier of the Amazon EC2 security group for the Amazon EMR service to access clusters in VPC private subnets.
---@field AdditionalMasterSecurityGroups? aws.emr.SecurityGroupsList A list of additional Amazon EC2 security group IDs for the master node.
---@field AdditionalSlaveSecurityGroups? aws.emr.SecurityGroupsList A list of additional Amazon EC2 security group IDs for the core and task nodes.

